    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **56 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature: `title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nChanges:\n- **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a persisted `title` column with getter/setter.\n- **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `title` column to the `owners` table in the hsqldb (used by tests), h2, mysql, and postgres `schema.sql` files, and inserted a `NULL` title value into the positional `owners` seed inserts in hsqldb `data.sql` (h2/postgres use explicit column lists, so no change needed there).\n- **OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added an input `title` field (enum `MR`/`MRS`/`MS`/`DR`) to `OwnerFields`, and a server-derived read-only `salutation` field to `Owner`. These regenerate the `OwnerDto`/`OwnerFieldsDto` at build time.\n- **`Salutation` util** (`util/Salutation.java`) \u2014 pure derivation matching the existing util pattern (`CustomerCode`, `Timezone`, etc.).\n- **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 mapped `salutation` via `Salutation.of(owner)`, mirroring the other derived fields.\n\nThe `title` flows request \u2192 entity via MapStruct (enum\u2192String) and persists, so the derived `salutation` is correct on both create and subsequent GET. The new `Cp45Tests` passes and no existing test regressed.",
